<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ferdinand I of Bulgaria</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1861–1948</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ferdinand I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a>, a German prince of the Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a> family, was elected prince of Bulgaria in 1887. In 1908 he declared full independence from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and took the title of tsar. He led Bulgaria into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkan-wars">Balkan Wars</a> and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-powers">Central Powers</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, and abdicated after defeat in 1918.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ferdinand-i-of-bulgaria.jpg" alt="Ferdinand I of Bulgaria" width="320" height="470" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zar_Ferdinand_Bulgarien.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
